-- a page made once for each state of the source (the view's stamp) and kept in the store as the
-- response's bytes (STORE/site-STAMP-KEY): the build makes every published page so (s-make-site), and
-- a reader is served the kept bytes; the response is written as it is made and then read back from
-- the file, so it is not held twice (Avik, 2026-11-18: "its mission critical this never goes down again")
s-site-or : List Word → Proc W (List Word) → Sum Unit (List Word) → Proc W (List Word)
s-site-or f mk (inr r) = ret {lzero} {W} r
s-site-or f mk (inl u) = bind mk (λ r → bind (h-write f r) (λ ok → if ok then bind (h-read f) (λ k → ret {lzero} {W} (s-or nil k)) else mk))
